{
  "id": "m10-weighted-completion",
  "title": "Weighted Completion Times",
  "source": {
    "name": "Smith's rule (weighted shortest processing time), a classic exchange-argument result"
  },
  "rating": 1500,
  "tags": [
    "greedy",
    "sorting",
    "exchange-argument"
  ],
  "statement": "A single machine must run `n` jobs one after another with no gaps. Job `i` takes `t_i` time units and has an importance weight `w_i`. If job `i` finishes at time `C_i`, the total cost is the sum of `w_i * C_i`. Choose the order that minimises this cost and print the minimum.\n\n**Input.** First line `n`. Then `n` lines `t_i w_i`.\n\n**Output.** The minimum total cost.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 800 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "1 ≤ t_i, w_i ≤ 10^5",
    "Costs can exceed 2^53; use 64-bit integers (BigInt in JavaScript)"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Try two jobs: when is running A before B cheaper than B before A?",
    "A before B costs `w_A t_A + w_B (t_A + t_B)`, B before A costs `w_B t_B + w_A (t_A + t_B)`. Compare them.",
    "A first is better iff `t_A * w_B < t_B * w_A`, i.e. smaller `t / w` first. Sort with this cross-multiplied comparator (avoid floats) and accumulate."
  ],
  "editorial": "For two adjacent jobs the rest of the schedule is unaffected by their order, and A before B is no worse iff `t_A / w_A <= t_B / w_B`. So any schedule with an adjacent pair out of ratio order can be improved (or kept equal) by swapping it; repeating until no adjacent inversion remains gives the schedule sorted by `t / w`, which is therefore optimal (all sorted orders have the same cost up to ties). Compare ratios by cross-multiplication to stay in integers. Time `O(n log n)`. The cost reaches about `4 * 10^16` for large inputs, beyond 2^53, so use `long` or BigInt.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\nfrom functools import cmp_to_key\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(d[0])\njobs = [(int(d[1 + 2 * i]), int(d[2 + 2 * i])) for i in range(n)]\n# sort by t / w using cross multiplication, then accumulate\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\n// then n lines 't w'; costs can pass 2^53, use BigInt\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        // use long for products and the cost\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n; cin >> n;  // read n pairs (t, w); sort by t / w without dividing\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nfrom functools import cmp_to_key\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(d[0])\njobs = [(int(d[1 + 2 * i]), int(d[2 + 2 * i])) for i in range(n)]\njobs.sort(key=cmp_to_key(lambda x, y: x[0] * y[1] - y[0] * x[1]))\ntime = 0\ncost = 0\nfor t, w in jobs:\n    time += t\n    cost += w * time\nprint(cost)\n",
    "javascript": "const lines = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) lines.push(line);\nconst tok = lines.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(s => s.length);\nconst n = Number(tok[0]);\nconst jobs = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < n; i++) jobs.push([Number(tok[1 + 2 * i]), Number(tok[2 + 2 * i])]);\njobs.sort((x, y) => x[0] * y[1] - y[0] * x[1]);\nlet time = 0n, cost = 0n;\nfor (const [t, w] of jobs) {\n  time += BigInt(t);\n  cost += BigInt(w) * time;\n}\nconsole.log(cost.toString());\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        long[][] jobs = new long[n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            jobs[i][0] = sc.nextLong();\n            jobs[i][1] = sc.nextLong();\n        }\n        Arrays.sort(jobs, (x, y) -> Long.compare(x[0] * y[1], y[0] * x[1]));\n        long time = 0, cost = 0;\n        for (long[] j : jobs) {\n            time += j[0];\n            cost += j[1] * time;\n        }\n        System.out.println(cost);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<pair<long long, long long>> jobs(n);\n    for (auto &j : jobs) cin >> j.first >> j.second;\n    sort(jobs.begin(), jobs.end(), [](const pair<long long, long long>& x, const pair<long long, long long>& y) {\n        return x.first * y.second < y.first * x.second;\n    });\n    long long time = 0, cost = 0;\n    for (auto &j : jobs) {\n        time += j.first;\n        cost += j.second * time;\n    }\n    cout << cost << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
